    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 all 26 tests pass, including the new `Cp16Tests` and `Cp09Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n- **`nextCustomerCode`** now takes both `city` and `lastName`. It builds `CITY3` from the upper-cased first three letters of the city, `LAST3` from the last name, and `NNNN` as a **per-city** 4-digit zero-padded sequence \u2014 one more than the number of owners already in that city (matched case-insensitively), replacing the previous global owner count.\n- Updated the call site (`createOwner`) and the surrounding doc comments to describe the new format (e.g. `SYD-SMI-0007`).\n\nNothing else needed to change for values derived from the customer code:\n- **Membership number** (`OwnerMapper.membershipNumber`) is built as `<customerCode>-M<YY>` directly from `getCustomerCode()`, so it automatically rebuilds on the new format \u2014 confirmed by the format-agnostic `Cp14Tests`.\n- Seed owners carry no `customer_code` (it's assigned only on create), so no seed/schema changes were required.",
